invariant: INV-26
file: aes.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh aes_runtime
reason: an AES=runtime QUIC object expands an Initial key on the AES
  instructions for every answer but 0, the absent one included, so a
  session whose caller's probe found none executes AES instructions
  before its first packet. The aes_runtime proof's stubs assert that only
  the answer present runs the instructions, over every byte an answer
  can be.

--- old
    if (aes_instructions == CH_AES_INSTRUCTIONS_PRESENT) {
--- new
    if (aes_instructions != 0) {
